% Every _ is a fresh variable (spec §9), so pair(_, _) must not force its two
% arguments to be equal.  Anonymous variables are never projected (spec §14),
% so a query over them answers true/false and two bindings that differ only
% in an anonymous column collapse to one row.
pair(a, b).
pair(c, c).

edge(a, b).
edge(a, c).

any(X) :- pair(X, _).

pair(_, _)?
edge(X, _)?
any(X)?
